{
 "about": "Title rules of the MBA role set, written by pipeline/roles_mba.py (do not edit by hand). Patterns are JavaScript regular expressions; use the 'i' flag. How to read a title: see 'how'.",
 "how": [
  "1. A title that matches 'junk' has no role.",
  "2. general = the first entry of 'families' with a match in 'patterns' and none in 'exclude'. An entry with 'product_gate' also needs the product rules to hold: product.family(title) equals the gate, and product.title_ok(title).",
  "3. When the employer's category is in 'employer_first' and general is not in 'named_first': use the employer rule (step 5) if it gives a role.",
  "4. When general is corp_dev, the employer is in 'banks' and the title does not say corporate development: the role is ib_associate. Otherwise the role is general.",
  "5. Employer rule, also the fallback when general is empty: at a consulting category, a title matching 'consultant' is management_consultant unless it matches 'consultant_exclude'. Otherwise no role when the title matches 'employer_exclude' (or 'real_estate_exclude' at a real-estate firm); else the first rule of 'employer_rules'[category] that matches.",
  "6. Level: pick the ladder ('ladders'.*.applies), replace a chief-of-staff phrase ('chief_of_staff') with 'CoS', then the first grade whose pattern matches; none: 'mid'. An ldp title with no manager word ('ldp_staff') is 'associate'."
 ],
